---
title: Ada Lovelace Builder Season
description: A public invitation to make something for Ada Lovelace Day.
layoutClass: event-landing
---

{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% set interestFormUrl = "https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfBwd6Prlmjro5J0YBd7CcBn1_N9dsWrqngFGZM_THZ_U07jg/viewform?usp=dialog" %}

{% block title %}Ada Lovelace Builder Season{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="ada-page">
  <section class="ada-hero" aria-labelledby="landing-title">
    <div class="ada-hero-copy">
      <p class="ada-kicker">Ada Lovelace Day Builder Season</p>
      <h2 id="landing-title">Make something. Finish it. Put it into the world.</h2>
      <p class="ada-lead">
        A Builder Season is a longer, more welcoming evolution of the hackathon:
        less weekend sprint, more sustained making, public progress, and finished work.
      </p>
      <div class="ada-actions">
        <a class="ada-btn ada-btn-primary" href="{{ interestFormUrl }}" rel="external noopener">
          Be notified when the Ada Lovelace Builder Season opens
        </a>
        <a class="ada-btn ada-btn-secondary" href="#how-it-works">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ada-machine" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="ada-sun"></div>
      <div class="ada-card-stack">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="ada-orbit">
        <span>01</span>
        <span>10</span>
        <span>11</span>
      </div>
      <p>Ada + imagination + machines</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="why" class="ada-band ada-band-light">
    <div class="ada-section-head">
      <p class="ada-kicker">Why Builder Season?</p>
      <h2>Hackathons create sparks. A season gives the spark somewhere to go.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ada-two-col">
      <p>
        Short competitive sprints are useful, but not every builder does their best work
        under a countdown clock. Builder Season makes room for learning, revision,
        collaboration, setbacks, persistence, and the very practical work of finishing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Building is broad here. Software counts. So do art, writing, research,
        educational material, events, media, performances, open-source contributions,
        experiments, and things nobody has a category for yet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="ada" class="ada-band ada-band-red">
    <div class="ada-section-head">
      <p class="ada-kicker">Why Ada Lovelace?</p>
      <h2>Poetical science is the theme.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ada-two-col">
      <p>
        Ada Lovelace saw computation as more than arithmetic. Her work joined
        mathematical precision with imagination, language, music, and the question of
        what machines might someday help people create.
      </p>
      <p>
        This season celebrates that combination, and the women in STEM and technology
        whose contributions deserve to be recognized, encouraged, and made visible now.
        For Cardano builders, ADA is more than a ticker. It is a name worth knowing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="ada-band">
    <div class="ada-section-head">
      <p class="ada-kicker">How It Works</p>
      <h2>Commit -> Build -> Share -> Finish -> Celebrate</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="ada-loop" aria-label="Builder Season loop">
      <li>
        <strong>Commit</strong>
        Choose something small enough to finish and meaningful enough to care about.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Build</strong>
        Work over time. Learn, test, revise, ask for help, and keep going.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Share</strong>
        Make progress visible. Notes, demos, sketches, failures, and discoveries all count.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Finish</strong>
        Put a real thing into the world, even if it is modest, rough, or version one.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Celebrate</strong>
        Gather around the finished work and the people who made it.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section id="build" class="ada-band ada-band-yellow">
    <div class="ada-section-head">
      <p class="ada-kicker">What Could You Make?</p>
      <h2>An invitation, not a narrow track list.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ada-tag-cloud" aria-label="Example project directions">
      <span>Software</span>
      <span>Art</span>
      <span>Writing</span>
      <span>Research</span>
      <span>Education</span>
      <span>Events</span>
      <span>Media</span>
      <span>Open source</span>
      <span>Storytelling</span>
      <span>Experiments</span>
    </div>
    <p class="ada-wide-copy">
      Explore Ada's ideas. Celebrate a woman working in technology. Highlight women
      contributing to Cardano or blockchain. Combine code with music, mathematics with
      storytelling, engineering with art, or teaching with public imagination.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="share" class="ada-band ada-band-light">
    <div class="ada-section-head">
      <p class="ada-kicker">Build In Public</p>
      <h2>The process is part of the season.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ada-two-col">
      <p>
        Participants share progress along the way. Not just the polished artifact:
        the sketches, questions, tradeoffs, strange detours, hard lessons, and moments
        when the idea finally starts to work.
      </p>
      <p>
        You choose the scope. The season asks you to finish it. Small finished projects
        are welcome because completion is the point, not maximum complexity.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="interest" class="ada-cta" aria-labelledby="interest-title">
    <div>
      <p class="ada-kicker">Coming Next</p>
      <h2 id="interest-title">Be notified when the Ada Lovelace Builder Season opens.</h2>
      <p>
        The season is still being organized. Sign up to be notified when registration form opens.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="ada-btn ada-btn-primary" href="{{ interestFormUrl }}" rel="external noopener">
      Open interest form
    </a>
  </section>
</div>
{% endblock %}
